<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48933" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĕbĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a village in Umbria</i>, now <i>Trevi</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Arn. 3, 122</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĕ-bĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Trebia</i>, <i>Trebian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 14, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">di,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 3, 126</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĕbĭāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Trebia</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 31</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĕbĭātes</span></b> ,
			um, m., <i>the inhabitants of
				Trebia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14, 19, §
		114</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
